;; What "this release may become the running system" means, as checkable data.
;;
;; Four independent questions -- threshold, revocation, monotonicity, freshness
;; -- because they fail separately and each one answers a different attack.
;; Roles are TUF's, on purpose: same threat model, reused rather than reinvented.
[{:db/id -1
  :aiueos.publisher/id :aiueos/default-publisher-trust
  :aiueos.publisher/source-files ["src/grant/publisher.cljk"]
  :aiueos.publisher/roles #{:root :targets :snapshot :timestamp}
  :aiueos.publisher/questions [:threshold :revocation :monotonic-sequence :freshness]
  :aiueos.publisher/attack-answered
  "{:threshold :one-stolen-key, :revocation :key-stolen-before-known,
    :monotonic-sequence :rollback-to-known-bug, :freshness :freeze}"
  :aiueos.publisher/decision-shapes #{:grant :deny}
  :aiueos.publisher/deny-reasons #{:below-threshold :key-revoked :key-not-in-root
                                   :sequence-not-monotonic :timestamp-expired
                                   :timestamp-missing :digest-mismatch :unknown-role
                                   :root-expired :no-signatures :threshold-unsatisfiable
                                   :freshness-undecidable}
  :aiueos.publisher/freshness-source "aiueos.clock/decide-freshness when state carries :clock"
  :aiueos.publisher/index-outside-bitmap-is-revoked? true
  :aiueos.publisher/root-rotation-requires-both-roots? true
  :aiueos.publisher/revocation-format "org-w3-vc-bitstring-status-list"
  :aiueos.publisher/ordering-plane "kotoba-lang/inga"
  :aiueos.publisher/artifact-addressing :content-addressed
  :aiueos.publisher/opens-non-goal
  "root ADR-2608012050 declined binary-cache substitution until publisher trust
   and revocation were modelled to component-admission standard. This contract
   is that model; the non-goal is reopened by ADR-2608153600."
  :aiueos.publisher/assurance-gaps
  ["Signature verification, status-list decoding and block retrieval are
    provider mechanism. This namespace consumes verified flags and a decoded
    bitmap; a provider that lies makes every verdict here wrong."
   "Freshness needs a reading to ACCEPT. A machine with only a build-stamp lower
    bound can still REJECT a stale release (:older-than-lower-bound) but denies
    anything it cannot decide (:freshness-undecidable) -- it never falls through
    to admitting. Closing the accept half needs a real reading (RTC or a signed
    timestamp), which aiueos.clock ranks but does not obtain."]}]
